␀␀state␀␀␀attributes␀␀unit_of_measurement␀/api/states/␀␀␀␀Sensor not found: ␀␀update check␀␀␀␀network: update check␀␀␀Spotify command␀network: Spotify command␀␀␀␀channel counts␀␀network: channel counts␀live streams␀␀␀␀network: live streams␀␀␀profile pictures␀␀␀␀network: profile pictures␀␀␀latest videos␀␀␀network: latest videos␀␀comments␀␀␀␀network: comments␀␀␀new video tracker␀␀␀network: new video tracker␀␀typical views␀␀␀network: typical views␀␀weather␀network: weather␀␀␀␀network: Home Assistant␀network: Spotify␀␀␀␀recent uploads␀␀network: recent uploads␀phone notifications␀network: phone notifications␀␀␀␀closing connections␀network: closing connections␀␀␀␀idle␀␀␀␀network: idle␀␀␀entity_id␀␀␀device_class␀␀␀␀friendly_name␀␀␀/api/states␀temperature␀humidity␀␀␀␀err␀Type the Home Assistant address and paste a token first.␀␀␀␀:8123␀␀␀nT␀␀nH␀␀. Is the address right? Home Assistant usually uses port 8123, e.g. http://192.168.1.20:8123␀␀␀␀Setup mode␀␀Scanning Wi-Fi...␀␀␀Connect it on the␀␀␀Nothing playing␀Start something on Spotify␀␀Check Spotify in settings␀␀␀Hold BOOT 1 s for the menu␀␀<b style='color:#30d158'>Installed &#10003;</b> The board is restarting &ndash; this page will go back to the dashboard in a few seconds.␀␀␀Updated!␀␀␀␀<b style='color:#ff3b30'>Not installed:</b> ␀␀␀␀no file received␀␀␀␀ The board is still running the old version.␀␀␀␀Update failed␀␀␀to v␀␀␀␀trying again␀␀␀␀Bad update address␀␀Download failed (␀␀␀Unexpected file size␀␀␀␀That isn't an APP-ONLY firmware file␀␀␀␀Download stopped at ␀␀␀␀Download failed (-␀␀ready␀␀␀unavailable␀ channels␀␀␀SubCounter v14.5 starting␀␀␀GMT0BST,M3.5.0/1,M10.5.0/2␀␀TZ␀␀spiffs␀␀/littlefs␀␀␀History storage %s
